label chapter_5_1:
    scene bg BATHROOM

    nvl clear

    shn "Everyone's feelings always feel so much stronger when we share in our joys and our sorrows... ♪"

    shn "If my voice can reach you, surely a miracle can happen―"

    shn "And I'll neeever forget the promises we exchanged... ♪"

    nvl clear

    n "The pen went scribbly-scribbly on the paper. It scratched so loud that I thought the paper was going to tear, but I controlled the pressure of my wrist best I could. I was drawing shokoichan, in her perfect form, all curves perfect and her face so cute you could never hate her. But those were underneath her armor―she's devilishly boyish on the outside. I leaned against the comfort room door, and I could hear some other girl taking a leak in the next stall. Not that it really mattered to me `cos I wasn't leaving here until I finished casting this spell. The smell of ammonia was getting on my nose's nerves, though, but that didn't matter in the moment, again."

    n "I flipped through my notebook looking for my other drawings of shokoichan. There I happened upon some old bad memories, and all I could really do was stare at it. There was dirt smudged on that page."

    nvl clear

    shn "This looks even worse than my drawings from last year... Ahahaha."

    n "I instinctively put my thumb on the crayon Sofia's face and it smudged. I was trying to give her a bit of a pet on the head y'know, but I realized that just ruined the pure page. Whatever childhood purity it had was gone, so I wanted to stop staring at it any longer. I flipped through all of my notebook pages one last time trying to get a glimpse of what it was I was looking for, and all I got were other half-finished drawings of shokoichan. Some of her trying to pose cutely, others with her head brutally cut off―I dunno and don't remember who drew those, but I kinda let them exist in the little crevices between my notebook. One of the pages was even coated in red, but they all had one thing in common, and it was that they were all undeniably insanely ugly. Like some kinda amateur drew them, or maybe even someone in kindergarten, not in highschool. Figures since people say I got the head of a preschooler on the body of a highschooler, though I always thought they were wrong, sometimes I think I get why people say the things they do about me. I flipped back to my current drawing and even that looked like utter dogshit. But only one thing mattered to me―and that's that she's cute!"

    nvl clear

    n "I flipped the notebook closed. It's got poked holes and chewed off bites on the cover, and I'm thinkin' that's because of the stray cat that comes in our little home sometimes. He's always way hungry and myaaaw myawing for more food, because he's never ever satisfied with what we give him. He probably went for my notebook. That's not good, though. He's gonna eat up all of my dreams and it's all gonna fall apart. Bad Mr. Kitty."

    nvl clear

    n "I swear the more I stood in the comfort room the more I could smell faint sewage, maybe shit and piss. Man, if only I saw the last girl that was in here. I could probably make some shitty rumors about her and have her see how it feels, haha. That's disgusting, that people can just live like that. Spreading rumors and having bad sanitary habits. I finished drawing shokoichan, and that was now the pictogram for the curse that was gonna befall this entire shitty, shitty school, and then the siokoy's gonna come and eat up everyone's dreams."

    nvl clear

    shn "......"

    shn "No matter how tall the wall, I'm definitely crossin' over it..."

    nvl clear

    n "I closed my eyes shut, real tight, and I imagined a flood washing over the school. The siokoy swam in the waters and gobbled everyone's heads up, and eventually the entire flood turned transparent red. The only one it didn't eat was me, `cus I could breathe in the water much like he can, so he recognized that I was a friend, one of his species. I smiled and shook the siokoy's hand, while Sofia's disembodied body floated around spewing blood from the headless neck. In my little vision, I declared the siokoy my new best friend, and that he was now my new Pomorimo-friend."

    n "Even though that should've been a happy thing to think, I couldn't really feel happy about it at all."

    return
